def scan_map[A: Movable & Deinitable, T: Movable & Deinitable, Y: Movable & Deinitable, V: Movable & Deinitable, R: Movable & Deinitable](var function: def(var A, var T) thin -> R, var initial: A, var source: V) -> ScanMapIterator[A, T, Y, _Source[V], def(var A, var T) thin -> R] where _Source[V].Element == T and R == Tuple[A, Y]:
    """Lazily consume (carry, input) into (new carry, output), yielding one output per input.

    Construction pulls nothing and there is no initial output. The carry need not be Copyable.
    Each non-raising step moves both arguments; output and carry may have different types.
    Exhaustion is fused. Abandonment releases carry, callback and source; final carry is not exposed.

    Parameters:
        A: The first callback argument type.
        T: The source element type, including origins.
        Y: The independent scan output type, including origins.
        V: The consumed native iterator or owned collection type.
        R: The callback result type.

    Args:
        function: The callback, borrowed or owned according to the selected overload; captures retain their native origins.
        initial: The initial carry, consumed; scan_map does not yield it.
        source: The source, consumed at its current position.

    Returns:
        ScanMapIterator[A, T, Y, _Source[V], def(var A, var T) thin -> R] with the ownership, timing and empty-input behavior described above.
    """
    return ScanMapIterator[A, T, Y, _Source[V], def(var A, var T) thin -> R](function, initial^, _source(source^), False, False)

